The attached image is a conceptual diagram illustrating the dendrimer-like structure of the Nano-11 nanoparticle. It visually represents the highly branched internal architecture, which is characteristic of phytoglycogen, the plant-derived a-D-glucan nanoparticle. As described in Figure 1 of the PDF, Nano-11 (PG-OS-CHPTAC) is chemically modified to acquire a positive surface charge, allowing for efficient electrostatic adsorption of negatively charged protein antigens like ovalbumin. This structure and surface property are crucial for Nano-11's function as an effective vaccine adjuvant, enhancing antigen delivery to dendritic cells and stimulating immune responses.